In message <cm6287$jqa$1@joe.rice.edu>, Andy Johnson wrote:
..
> I like this way more, but it would allow two (possibly consecutive) 
> games to be nearly identical just by altering the gender. It'd be better 
> to just say no two of which have the same alignment, race, and role, or 
> maybe even just no two of which have the same race and role.

I concur that gender seems to be largely unimportant to the actual game
mechanics (apparently, the nymphs are all bisexual).  The game has it, though,
and considers it a fundamental character attribute and we do generally try to
follow the game's lead on such things.

It may allow a player to ascend what are basically 6 pairs of _very_ similar
characters, but I think that's acceptible.  It still leaves some flexibility
for the player to choose the style they prefer.

We do already have two other trophies that do much as you suggest and are
_very_ strict that the player must ascend one game with every possible
fundamental attribute.

We will definitely keep an eye on how folks approach the Best of 13 trophy,
though, and if it looks like there's no real variety in how it's approached
we'll cghange it for next year.

-robin

